      "script": [
        "*Evening. The room is quiet. Bram wipes the same mug over and over.*",
        "I wasn't always a cook, {player}. I guarded caravans for twelve years.",
        "One night we were ambushed on the pass. I lost four friends. I walked away with a limp and a nightmare.",
        {
          "say": "That's why I'm here. I wanted to build somewhere nobody has to be afraid on the road.",
          "choices": [
            {
              "text": "You've built exactly that.",
              "reply": [
                "*He sets down the mug. His eyes are shiny.* Hm. Maybe I have."
              ],
              "points": 70
            },
            {
              "text": "Tell me their names.",
              "reply": [
                "*He tells you. All four. Slowly.*",
                "Nobody's asked in years. Thank you."
              ],
              "points": 80
            },
            {
              "text": "That's the past. Move on.",
              "reply": [
                "*He goes back to wiping the mug.* Easy to say."
              ],
              "points": -30
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
